  "result": "Excellent! I've added voucher support to the invoicing system. Here's what was implemented:\n\n## Updated `src/invoices.js`\n\n- **`applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })`** \u2014 Applies a fixed-amount voucher to a draft invoice:\n  - Only works on draft invoices (returns `NOT_DRAFT` error otherwise)\n  - Only one voucher per invoice (returns `VOUCHER_EXISTS` if already has one)\n  - Amount must be a positive integer in cents (returns `AMOUNT_INVALID` if not)\n  - Sets `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n  - Returns `ok(newInvoice)` without mutating the original\n\n- **Updated `invoiceTotals()`** to include vouchers:\n  - Returns a `voucher` field (the amount from the voucher, or 0)\n  - Recalculates total as: `subtotal - discount + vat - voucher`\n  - All amounts remain in cents and clamped to 0 minimum\n\n## Updated `src/errors.js`\n\nAdded error code:\n- `VOUCHER_EXISTS` \u2014 An invoice can only have one voucher.\n\n## Added 9 tests to `test/invoices.test.js`\n\n- Voucher added to draft invoice\n- Voucher reduces total correctly\n- NOT_DRAFT error for non-draft invoices\n- VOUCHER_EXISTS error when one already applied\n- AMOUNT_INVALID errors (zero, negative, non-integer amounts)\n- Immutability of original invoice\n- invoiceTotals includes voucher field with correct calculation\n\n**All 171 tests pass** (9 new + 162 existing).",
